  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving  women Access to Land in selected  rural communities in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at working with stakeholders at all levels to ensure improved women&#x2019;s access to land through research, sensitization and awareness raising and advocacy. In Sierra Leone women have been discriminated against in access to land in most of the rural areas, which has deprived women of their livelihood options and as such, they have continued to live in abject poverty. In 2007, the government brought in a piece of legislation known as the &#x201c;Devolution of Estate Act 2007&#x201d;</narrative>
  </description>
